   "sentenceId": 3,
   "he": "הַשּׁוֹחֵט וְנִמְצֵאת טְרֵיפָה וְכוּ׳. אֲמַר לֵיהּ רַב חֲבִיבִי מָחוֹזְנָאָה לְרַב אָשֵׁי: שְׁמַע מִינַּהּ, אֵינָהּ לִשְׁחִיטָה אֶלָּא לְבַסּוֹף.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: A thief «who slaughters» the animal «but it was found to be a tereifa,» and likewise a thief who slaughters a non-sacred animal in the Temple courtyard, pays the fourfold or fivefold payment. «Rav Ḥavivi of Meḥoza said to Rav Ashi: Conclude from» the mishna that the act «of slaughtering» is considered to have been performed «only at the end» of the slaughtering process."
  }
